        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="HAR03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Thomas</forename>
                        <surname>Harris</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1820-10-01"/>
                    <occupation>theatre manager</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Harris replaced George Colman the Elder as manager of Covent Garden theatre in 1774. He remained manager until his death in 1820. He had a number of dealings 
    with Godwin regarding the latter's plays but he never accepted any of them for performance.</p>
                        <p>Only those instances of Harris which can be definitely taken to be Thomas have been coded. There are a number of Harris's 
  which may be Thomas Harris but due to 1) the common nature of the surname and 2) the fact that there are instances of Harris which post-date his death, 
  these have been left uncoded.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 1, fol. 19: 19 October 1804</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
